      "description": "Watch New England Revolution vs Atlanta United FC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. The MLS clash between New England Revolution and Atlanta United FC offered a masterclass in attacking football, with both teams trading blows throughout the encounter. Played on July 26, 2026, the game was defined by clinical finishing and a dramatic sequence of events that swung the momentum multiple times. Early Breakthrough and First Half Battle New England Revolution wasted no time in asserting their dominance at home. Just 11 minutes into the match, Carles Gil found the back of the net following a clever assist from Matt Polster . The early goal ignited the crowd, but Atlanta United remained composed under pressure. Despite yellow cards for Alhassan Yusuf and Matthew Edwards , the visitors found their rhythm. In the 36th minute, Dor Turgeman leveled the score, expertly finishing a pass from Alhassan Yusuf to ensure the sides went into the break on even terms. Second Half Seesaw The intensity only increased after the restart. In the 56th minute, the hosts regained the lead when Peyton Miller struck, with Alhassan Yusuf once again involved in the build-up. However, the lead proved fragile. Atlanta United responded within minutes; in the 67th minute, Brooklyn Raines capitalized on an assist from substitute Jackson Yueill to make it 2-2. The match became a tactical chess match as both managers turned to their benches, looking for a decisive edge. Almiron Seals the Win With the match entering its final stages, it was the visitors who found the moment of magic. In the 85th minute, Miguel Almiron proved his worth by scoring the winning goal, set up by a precise assist from Aleksey Miranchuk . Despite several minutes of added time and desperate late pressure from the New England Revolution , Atlanta United held firm to claim all three points in a thrilling encounter that will be remembered as a classic of the 2026 season."
